  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Triple Canopy obligated $324M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Triple Canopy received 66 awards in the same period, with an average award size of $4.9M, and obligations fell 14.6% year over year. Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, obligating $221M, followed by Department of State with $91.7M and Department of Defense with $11.6M. Security Guards and Patrol Services is Triple Canopy's dominant market with $282M in obligations, followed by Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) at $23.6M, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $15.6M, and Engineering Services at $3.1M. Historical obligations show higher totals in prior years, with FY21 at $479M, FY22 at $382M, FY23 at $468M, FY24 at $478M, and FY25 at $380M. The current-year total is a fiscal year to date partial sum. Use these topline figures to compare program scale, client mix, and market concentration when preparing bids, staffing plans, or risk assessments for work with Triple Canopy.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Triple Canopy's federal revenue trended over recent years?",
        "body": "Triple Canopy's obligations have varied year to year, with FY21 at $479M, FY22 at $382M, FY23 at $468M, FY24 at $478M, FY25 at $380M, and FY26 at $324M. Triple Canopy's obligations fell 14.6% year over year into FY26 to date. Triple Canopy's current-year total is a fiscal year to date partial sum, not a full-year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Triple Canopy's main customers and what markets drive its business?",
        "body": "Department of Homeland Security, Department of State, and Department of Defense are the top buyers, obligating $221M, $91.7M, and $11.6M respectively in FY2026 to date. Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest market at $282M, with Security Systems Services at $23.6M and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $15.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
